# Corner Analysis

1H/2H splits are **statistical** (team half-split ratios + trained models). Never hard-code 50/50 or “more corners after half-time”.

Read `ReadMeDocs/CORNER_PREDICTIONS_GUIDE.md`, `ReadMeDocs/WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md`, and skill `corner-prediction`. There is no `CORNERS_ANALYSIS_FLOW.md` — use those docs plus `SCRIPT_FLOW_DIAGRAM.md`.

## Scripts

- `corners_analysis.py` — features, correlations, team stats, single-match predict, `--train-model`
- `automate_corner_predictions.py` — batch from a match log (preferred for multi-match)

```bash
python cli.py --task corners --use-parsed-all --min-team-matches 5 --corners-use-ml-prediction --verbose
python cli.py --task corners --input tmp/corners/YYMMDD_match_games.log --leagues E2,E3 --train-model --force --auto --mode fast
```

## Rules

- Skip teams below `--min-team-matches` (default 5).
- `--use-parsed-all` processes only leagues present in `todays_fixtures_*`.
- Outputs go to `data/corners/` (`parsed_corners_predictions_*.json`, `batch_predictions_*.json`).
- Prefer `--mode fast` (cached team stats) unless the user asks for a full rebuild.
- Monte Carlo ranges: `--corners-mc-samples` default 1000.
